  "method": "Each mutant replaces `old` with `new` (exactly one occurrence) in one file of the S6 worktree at `commit`, runs `command` from the worktree root, then restores the file; the tree was clean after the run. A mutant is killed only when the replacement applied and the command exits nonzero.",
  "history": "A first run at the pre-amend commit left M30 (the policy bytes read for the screen not compared with the act) surviving: the act chain already compares the bytes it reads, so no test changed the policy between that read and the screen's own. loadDossierScreen took an injectable byte reader and a test that changes the bytes between the two reads; the commit was amended and all 30 re-run. After the rulings (a)-(d), a run of 44 at the next pre-amend commit (e347db7d) left two surviving: M32, which then removed an `isAbsolute` clause made redundant by the `path.resolve(p) !== p` clause beside it (an equivalent mutant; the redundant clause was removed and M32 now removes the resolve clause), and M44, because no test located a quotation inside text a normalisation step carries over (the text of a link, an escaped character). Tests for that origin and for a clone path with a NUL or past 4096 characters were added, M45 (the NUL clause) was added, the commit was amended and all 45 re-run. S6 was then rebased onto the step-guard repair (syzygy-qkea.23, PR #379): its clone-recording hunk merged into the identical one in #379, `check` passes its object reader and the guard's machine refusals through, and M26's `old` fragment follows the new refusal block; all 45 were re-run. After #379 merged with its round-2 repair (the provider compared with the brief record, which changes brief.ts, a subject here), S6 was rebased onto main, keeping both clone real-path tests, and all 45 were re-run at `commit`.",
